## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a streaming NLP system that handles multiple languages, domain adaptation, drift monitoring, latency budgets, and privacy considerations.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual NER with adapters
- Drift monitoring and active learning
- Domain gazetteers and retrieval augmentation
- Privacy: data minimization and differential privacy
- Evaluation: streaming metrics, latency budgets, OOD checks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-inference sketch with adapters
async function predict(text, model) {
  const tokens = tokenize(text);
  const enc = model.encode(tokens);
  const logits = await model.predict(enc);
  return decodeEntities(logits, tokens);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you quantify and react to drift in production?
- How would you structure the entity schema with provenance and versioning?
- How would you audit and mitigate bias across languages?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests end-to-end NLP system design with real-world constraints including fast latency, multilingual support, and explainability in a developer documentation context.

## Key Concepts
- Hybrid retrieval combining dense (neural) and lexical (BM25) approaches
- Intent and slot extraction for query understanding
- Latency targets with p95 guarantees (<150ms)
- Privacy-preserving query handling via hashing
- Explainability through token contribution scoring

## Code Example
```javascript
function extractIntentAndSlots(query) {
  const intents = ['info', 'api', 'example'];
  const slots = ['language', 'framework', 'version'];
  // Lightweight classifier implementation
  return { intent: classify(query, intents), slots: extract(query, slots) };
}

async function hybridRetrieve(query, k=10) {
  const denseResults = await denseSearch(query, k);
  const bm25Results = await bm25Search(query, k);
  return fuseResults(denseResults, bm25Results);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor drift in documentation relevance over time?
- What strategies would you use to handle low-resource languages?
- How would you implement the query hashing for privacy while maintaining search quality?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design end-to-end NLP systems at the edge with privacy, latency, and explainability constraints. This scenario blends multilingual NL understanding, policy translation, and auditable versioning in a cloud-edge ecosystem.

## Key Concepts

- Multilingual intent classification at edge with latency constraints
- Policy translation to concrete firewall/CDN rules with a grammar-based bridge
- Explainability and privacy controls with audit trails in MongoDB

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: mapNLToPolicy NL -> RuleSet
function mapNLToPolicy(nl, locale) {
  const intent = classifyIntent(nl, locale);
  const rules = translateIntentToRules(intent);
  return { intent, rules };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate rule safety before deployment at the edge?
- What drift-detection signals would you monitor and how would you rollback?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests your ability to design a practical, privacy-preserving NLP feature for multilingual chat environments. It evaluates understanding of on-device processing constraints, entity normalization challenges, and real-world deployment considerations for streaming platforms.

## Key Concepts
- Hybrid detection: lexicon-based pattern matching + lightweight ML classifier
- On-device inference with privacy-by-design architecture
- Multilingual text processing and code-switching tolerance
- Active learning for continuous data labeling and improvement
- Phased evaluation: offline metrics, shadow testing, staged rollout

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: hybrid entity detection approach
function extractEntity(tokens, lexicon, model) {
  // Fast lexicon lookup first
  const matches = lexiconLookup(tokens);
  if (matches.length > 0) {
    return normalizeEntities(matches);
  }
  // Fallback to lightweight classifier
  const predictions = model.predict(tokens);
  return filterByConfidence(predictions);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests building lightweight, on-device NLP under strict memory and latency constraints, handling code-switching and multilingual input.

## Key Concepts
- On-device NLP, memory budgeting, latency targets
- Code-switching handling with language routing
- Lightweight lexical resources plus small ML fallback

## Code Example
```javascript
function correctWord(word, dict) {
  // simple one-edit distance correction
  if (dict.has(word)) return word;
  // naive neighbor search: insert/delete/replace
  // (illustrative; real impl would be optimized)
  for (const w of dict) {
    if (levDistance(word, w) <= 1) return w;
  }
  return word;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate the system for drift and multilingual coverage over time?
- How would labeling and rollout be coordinated with very small devices in production?
